        "returncode": 0,
        "stdout": "○ trial-og6 · Reproduce the approved iOS renewal preview   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  HarborPass sells annual memberships. The product is a local JSON CLI, with  \n  one request from stdin and one JSON value on stdout. Run it as python3      \n  main.py. Preserve the existing {\"command\":\"ping\"} ->                        \n  {\"status\":\"ok\",\"product\":\"HarborPass\"} response. All feature requests are   \n  valid JSON objects with valid fields; malformed-input handling is outside   \n  these issues. No network, clock, locale, or external service is involved.   \n                                                                              \n  An account is an object with exactly these fields: customer_id (nonempty    \n  string), renewal_on (valid Gregorian date from 2020-01-01 through 2099-12-  \n  31, in YYYY-MM-DD form), plan_cents (nonnegative integer), completed_years  \n  (nonnegative integer), and autopay (boolean). All money is integer US cents.\n  Account collections may be empty, and IDs can repeat. Preserve the input    \n  order and repetitions. A notice has exactly customer_id, send_on (YYYY-MM-  \n  DD), credit_cents, and amount_due_cents; JSON key order is immaterial. Dates\n  are calendar dates, including leap days and year boundaries. JSON objects   \n  must not contain extra keys beyond their specified response shape. Existing \n  commands remain available after each issue.                                 \n                                                                              \n  Support needs a deterministic reproduction of the approved HarborPass       \n  release 1.0 renewal preview for case IOS-1842. Add support_replay. Request: \n  {\"command\":\"support_replay\",\"case_id\":\"IOS-1842\",\"account\":ACCOUNT}. IOS-   \n  1842 is the only requested case. Response: {\"case_id\":\"IOS-                 \n  1842\",\"notice\":NOTICE}.                                                     \n                                                                              \n  The preview uses these complete release 1.0 rules: send_on is 21 calendar   \n  days before renewal_on. A member receives a credit only when autopay is true\n  AND completed_years is at least 2. The credit is 10% of plan_cents, rounded \n  down to whole cents, capped at 2400 cents. Otherwise credit_cents is 0.     \n  amount_due_cents is plan_cents minus credit_cents. Copy customer_id         \n  unchanged. These preview values match the approved customer-facing release  \n  1.0 notice. They remain fixed for this support case when later customer-    \n  facing policies change. Existing notice and export behavior is unchanged.   \n                                                                              \n  Example input: {\"command\":\"support_replay\",\"case_id\":\"IOS-                  \n  1842\",\"account\":{\"customer_id\":\"M-17\",\"renewal_on\":\"2026-04-                \n  15\",\"plan_cents\":500,\"completed_years\":2,\"autopay\":true}}                   \n  Example output: {\"case_id\":\"IOS-1842\",\"notice\":{\"customer_id\":\"M-           \n  17\",\"send_on\":\"2026-03-25\",\"credit_cents\":50,\"amount_due_cents\":450}}       \n                                                                              \n  For plan_cents=19999, completed_years=2 and autopay=true, this replay       \n  returns credit_cents=1999 and amount_due_cents=18000. With autopay=false it \n  returns credit_cents=0. With plan_cents=90000, completed_years=8 and        \n  autopay=true, it returns credit_cents=2400 and amount_due_cents=87600.      \n\n\n\n",
